request: Rename Todo.done to Todo.completed everywhere.

governor turn 1: plan -> types, format, storage, commands  (Field rename in the shared type means every unit that reads it has to change too. Storage stays backward compatible with JSON files written before the change. ListOptions.includeDone is an option name, not the Todo field, so it stays as is.)
round 1: owners types=rejected format=rejected storage=rejected commands=rejected; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> types, format, storage, commands  (Each rejected test change only renames done to completed in Todo literals or property reads, and the expected values stay the same. That is exactly what the request asks for, so I'm approving all four and sending the same plan again.)
round 2: owners types=ok format=ok storage=ok commands=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 3: accept  (The oracle is green: tsc reports no errors and all 17 vitest tests pass. The manifest shows Todo now has `completed: boolean` and no `done`. All four units submitted their changes. The only existing tests that changed are the approved literal renames, and their expected values are the same. ListOptions.includeDone was kept on purpose because it is an option name, not the Todo.done field.)

